From 03ba56d01036e24a320f1e357a3acfa4fe72d7bb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mei Tanaka <mei.tanaka@example.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 10:05:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] test(policies): describe built-in routing verdicts as
 pytest-bdd scenarios (#8061)

Policy authors and operators kept asking what deny_trivial_to_expensive_model
actually does in each situation, and the answer lived in unit-test
docstrings. Describe its verdicts as Gherkin scenarios under
tests/policies/builtins/features/, run by pytest-bdd, so the behaviour
reads as a spec and product can review it without reading Python.

Adds pytest-bdd to the test group and documents the convention in
CONTRIBUTING.md: verdict changes to a built-in policy get a scenario,
helpers and registry entries stay in plain pytest.

Signed-off-by: Mei Tanaka <mei.tanaka@example.com>
